<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕgăris</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρίς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A country of Greece, between Attica and Phocis</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Mel.
				2, 3, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7, 11, §
			23</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city of Sicily, also called</i> Megara, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 25, § 63</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 8, 14, § 89</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
